ATTENDEE;CN="Darren Jew";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="admin@moretonbayfounda
 tion.org";ROLE=CHAIR:mailto:admin@moretonbayfoundation.org
ATTENDEE;CN="David Schoeman";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="dschoema@usc.edu.a
 u";PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT:mailto:dschoema@usc.edu.au
CREATED:20260506T225433Z
DESCRIPTION:CAUTION:This is an external email. Please take care when sel
 ecting links or opening attachments. When in doubt\, please contact the 
 IT Service Desk or IT Student Help Desk.\n2026 Q2: Bay Leadership Forum\
 n*** IMPORTANT NOTE: a MS Teams link will be sent 2 hours before the mee
 ting.If you have not RSVP'd "YES" to this Invitation you will NOT receiv
 e the link***We're pleased to confirm that our next onlin\n\nThis event 
 has been updated\nChanged: description\n\nDescription\nCHANGED\n\n*** IM
 PORTANT NOTE: a MS Teams link will be sent 2 hours before the meeting.\n
 If you have not RSVP'd "YES" to this Invitation you will NOT receive the
  link***\n\nWe're pleased to confirm that our next online meeting will t
 ake place on:\n\nDate: Thursday 28 May\nTime: 3:00 PM – 5:00 PM (via Tea
 ms)\n\nDear Bay Leaders\,\n\nWe look forward to seeing you at the Q2 202
 6 Bay Leaders Meeting.\n\nPlease see the Agenda below.\n\n3:00pm    Ackn
 owledgement of Country\n\n3:10pm    DEEP DIVES with Q&A:\n\n1. Greg Fisk
 \, Senior Advisor (EIS and approvals) Port of Brisbane\nUpdates on the C
 hannel Enhancement Project: including the overall program and expected t
 iming for the project approval process\; overview of studies and monitor
 ing underway\; changes to and refinement of the project design\, and how
  to find out more / engage with the EIS process\n\n2. Professor David Sc
 hoeman\, University of the Sunshine Coast\nHow can we conserve marine bi
 odiversity under climate change?\nWith climate change impacting marine b
 iodiversity throughout the global ocean\, conventional approaches to con
 servation planning may be inadequate. We identify areas of slowest envir
 onmental change across Australia’s marine estate and discuss associated 
 implications for marine conservation.\n\n3.  Dr Iris Tsoi Healthy Land a
 nd Water\n25 years of environmental data for South East Queensland: Repo
 rt Card 2025\nThe value of the regional long-term monitoring program has
  never been clearer\, with 25 years of data and insights supporting deci
 sion makers with the knowledge they need to drive resilient\, healthy re
 gions. Dr Tsoi will discuss the findings from the most recent Report Car
 d and what they mean for Moreton Bay.\n\n4. Associate Professor Alexandr
 a Campbell\, University of the Sunshine Coast\nSeaweed as a nutrient off
 set for Moreton Bay: a collaboration between researchers\, farmers\, Tra
 ditional Owners and water utilities.\nThe restorative aquaculture of sea
 weeds is often promoted as a solution to the climate crisis and other an
 thropogenic challenges. Established aquaculture farmers are increasingly
  interested in options to diversify revenue streams and enhance the sust
 ainability of their operations. Water utilities appreciate the co-benefi
 ts of restorative works that offset their operations. Traditional Owners
  are interested in activities that support communities on Country and si
 multaneously\, care for Country. This talk will detail the initial steps
  taken to understand the potential for seaweed production in Moreton Bay
 \, through joint research supported by the University of the Sunshine Co
 ast (UniSC)\, Urban Utilities (UU) and Moreton Bay Rock Oysters (MBRO)\,
  with co-funding from the Fisheries Research and Development Corporation
 \, in partnership with Quandamooka Yoolooburrabee Aboriginal Corporation
  (QYAC). I will share findings from the first trials of seaweed farming 
 off the coast of the State\, discuss the technical challenges involved\,
  and explore the opportunity for seaweed farming to help mitigate some e
 nvironmental challenges from urbanisation – including the emission of nu
 trients from our coastline.\n\n5. Katie Walters (CEO)\nTMBF Program upda
 tes\n\n6. Any other business\n\n4:50pm    Close\n\nCheers\,\n\nBest rega
 rds\,\nTMBF team.\n\nWhen\nThursday May 28\, 2026 ⋅ 3pm – 5pm (Australia
 n Eastern Standard Time - Brisbane)\nOrganiser\nDarren Jew<mailto:admin@
 moretonbayfoundation.org>\nadmin@moretonbayfoundation.org<mailto:admin@m
 oretonbayfoundation.org>\nGuests\n(Guest list has been hidden at organis
 er's request)\nReply for dschoema@usc.edu.au<mailto:dschoema@usc.edu.au>
 \n<https://aus01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcal
 endar.google.com%2Fcalendar%2Fevent%3Faction%3DRESPOND%26eid%3DNDIzcGxuY
 XBtOGZ1azdoZzU3OWczM2UwbWcgZHNjaG9lbWFAdXNjLmVkdS5hdQ%26rst%3D1%26tok%3D
 MzAjYWRtaW5AbW9yZXRvbmJheWZvdW5kYXRpb24ub3JnZjJkYmE0NjViMzVlYTdhMGEwYTcy
 ODcxZWRhODkwYTI1NDBjNzNmNA%26ctz%3DAustralia%252FBrisbane%26hl%3Den_GB%2
 6es%3D0&data=05%7C02%7Cdschoema%40usc.edu.au%7Cf608c9ccc57544d4e35f08deb
 56ffb7b%7C93b0ec50fc3f47ed93459ffc6012541c%7C0%7C0%7C639147689888710810%
